# The ancillary directory and the upload tarball are rebuilt wholesale from the
# already-tracked code/ and runs/ on every run of tools/make-arxiv.sh, so
# tracking them would duplicate ~300 KB of blobs per regeneration.
#
# There is a second reason, and it is the load-bearing one: anc/runs/ is a
# verbatim copy of runs/, and the global *.log / *.out / *.toc patterns above
# would silently drop any transcript so named -- producing a bundle missing a
# file the manuscript cites, with nothing to indicate it.  No current transcript
# matches, so this is prophylaxis rather than a fix, but the failure it prevents
# is invisible.
/article/arxiv/anc/
/article/arxiv/submission.tar.gz

# Lean build artefacts and fetched dependencies. .lake holds ~1.3 GB of cloned
# packages (mathlib, batteries, aesop, ...) each with its own .git, so committing
# it both bloats the repo and creates embedded repositories git cannot handle.
# lake-manifest.json + lean-toolchain are what actually pin the build.
LEAN/.lake/
.lake/
